  "pom_about_screen_footer_description": "An app for organizing your entire storage, powered by the best parts recognition technology there are",
  "@pom_about_screen_footer_description": {},
  "pom_about_screen_footer_title": "Pileometer by Brickit",
  "@pom_about_screen_footer_title": {},
  "pom_about_screen_list_item_1": "The app always knows exactly which bag contains the piece you need — and how many you have.",
  "@pom_about_screen_list_item_1": {},
  "pom_about_screen_list_item_2": "Transparent bags make things surprisingly easy: you spot the part instantly and grab it without hassle.",
  "@pom_about_screen_list_item_2": {},
  "pom_about_screen_list_item_3": "You’ll know right away if you have enough parts for any design from our extensive catalog.",
  "@pom_about_screen_list_item_3": {},
  "pom_about_screen_list_item_4": "You can quickly check if your collection has the pieces needed to rebuild any missing set.",
  "@pom_about_screen_list_item_4": {},
  "pom_about_screen_list_item_5": "You can import your collection into popular build-design websites to see how it matches the ideas you love.",
  "@pom_about_screen_list_item_5": {},
  "pom_about_screen_store_btn": "Try today",
  "@pom_about_screen_store_btn": {},
  "pom_about_screen_text_1": "We believe that any pile of boxes filled with bricks holds incredible potential for play, learning, and creativity. But first, it needs to become a collection — a structured, accessible, and familiar set of parts.",
  "@pom_about_screen_text_1": {},
  "pom_about_screen_text_2": "That’s why we built an app for exactly that. Meet Pile[o]meter.",
  "@pom_about_screen_text_2": {},
  "pom_about_screen_text_3": "Pile[o]meter is an app that combines the state-of-the-art Brickit scanner and a vast catalog of building ideas with a specially designed storage system. Getting started takes just two steps:",
  "@pom_about_screen_text_3": {},
  "pom_about_screen_text_4": "Scan your parts, batch by batch.",
  "@pom_about_screen_text_4": {},
  "pom_about_screen_text_5": "Sort them into numbered bags.",
  "@pom_about_screen_text_5": {},
  "pom_about_screen_text_6": "After that, everything becomes simple:",
  "@pom_about_screen_text_6": {},
  "pom_about_screen_title": "Catalog every part you have. Build bigger",
  "@pom_about_screen_title": {},
  "pom_bad_scan_btn_learn": "Open scanning tips",
  "@pom_bad_scan_btn_learn": {},
  "pom_bad_scan_btn_retake": "Retake photo",
  "@pom_bad_scan_btn_retake": {},
  "pom_bad_scan_btn_scan": "Proceed anyway",
  "@pom_bad_scan_btn_scan": {},
  "pom_bad_scan_text": "Brickit’s scanning technology relies heavily on a correctly taken photo. Check out our guide to improve your results.",
  "@pom_bad_scan_text": {},
  "pom_bad_scan_title": "The photo seems off",
  "@pom_bad_scan_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_done_btn": "Close",
  "@pom_education_screen_done_btn": {},
  "pom_education_screen_next_step_btn": "Next",
  "@pom_education_screen_next_step_btn": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_1_text": "Spread your parts in a single layer, making sure they don’t overlap. 150 to 250 pieces is the ideal amount for one scan.",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_1_text": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_1_title": "1. No Overlapping",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_1_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_2_text": "Ensure all key distinct features of each part are facing up so the app can recognize them accurately.",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_2_text": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_2_title": "2. Features Facing Up",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_2_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_3_text": "Use a clean, bright background that’s large enough. Two sheets of printer paper (8.5\" × 11\") work great!",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_3_text": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_3_title": "3. Clean Background",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_3_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_4_text": "Make sure the lighting is bright and even. Distinguishing between similar parts isn’t easy, and good lighting makes a difference.",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_4_text": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_4_title": "4. Good Lighting",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_4_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_5_text": "Take the photo directly from above. Get as close as possible so the parts fill most of the frame.",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_5_text": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_5_title": "5. Proper Angle",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_5_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_6_text": "Hold your phone steady while taking the photo to avoid blur. The sharper the image, the better the scanning accuracy!",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_6_text": {},
  "pom_education_screen_step_6_title": "6. Steady Shot",
  "@pom_education_screen_step_6_title": {},
  "pom_education_screen_title": "Scanning Guide",
  "@pom_education_screen_title": {},
  "pom_finder_back_btn": "Back to",
